Track 2: Skagerrak Skram
- Story & Context: Written in a sweat-drenched, unheated ferry terminal off the coast of Denmark, this track details the legendary night lead singer Freja Sol traded her winter coat for a bright yellow Hawaiian shirt and led a crowd of three hundred hypothermic punks in a daylight-simulated rave. The music relies on a frantic, non-English chant ("Skagerrak Skram!") lifted from North Sea radio slang for high-salinity seawater hitting hot engine pipes. A wall of distorted guitar octave-leads slams directly into an uplifting 909 trance drop as the crowd breaks the wooden floorboards. "Drink the salt, break the glass, summer isn't coming back so we bring it ourselves!"
