Track 3: The Stained Glass Solarium
- Story & Context: Long after the original pirate lighthouse broadcasts were shut down by Scandinavian communications authorities, this track stands as the mythic anthem of the Sunbreaker subculture, recorded using the salvaged glass fragments of the destroyed Vardø transmitter. Recorded live in one take with a single room mic catching both the pounding synth bass and the sound of waves crashing outside, it resolves the EP's frenetic energy into a sweeping, triumphant marine epic. Today, sunbreaker ravers play the song at dawn on northern beaches, smashing glass bottles against rocks as the final chorus hits. "Leave the broken frames behind, we are building a summer out of splinters!"
